  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Rehabilitation and Community-Based Reintegration Processes in Nigeria, with a Regional Approach-Phase Two</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen the capacity of the Federal Government of Nigeria (GoN) - Operation Safe Corridor (OPSC) to effectively implement rehabilitation programming as well as prepare host communities for sustainable community-based reintegration processes, with an improved Lake Chad Basin (LCB) countries regional coordination. This will be achieved through enhancing OPSC medical, nutritional and vocational training services to beneficiaries; Improving community support levels for the reintegration of Non-State Armed Groups (NSAG) associates and increasing cooperation among the LCB countries in reintegration and reconciliation programming.</narrative>
  </description>
